### Challenge 1: [Brief descriptive title]

**What I was trying to do:**
I needed to filter my data to remove underscores because aftet topic modeling the woman citizen data I found that my top term was _d. This is most likely due to a noisy OCR issue.

**What went wrong:**
I was not sure how to filter for non-words. 

**Did you use AI to troubleshoot this challenge?** [Yes / No] Yes


---

#### If YES, I used AI:

**My prompt to AI:**
```How do I filter to remove _d from my term results in twc.topics?
```

**AI's response:**
```r
#to clean this up, and to remove special characters like underscores, add another filter to only keep words that contain letters (and maybe apostrophes).
tidy_twc <- tidy_twc %>% 
  filter(!grepl('[0-9]', word)) %>%
  filter(str_detect(word, "^[a-z']+$")) %>%
  # ensures that words only containing lowercase letters and apostrophes from start to end.
  filter(!word %in% c("a'noted","ing"))  # I had to add another filter to get rid of other noisy OCR issues. This one exclude this term which was dominating my results and most likely is an abbreviation of "annotated".
   
```

**How I evaluated the AI's suggestion:**

**What I implemented and why:**
I thought through the code first to see if it was reasonable. Then, I ran it and looked at the tidy_twc dataframe to see if it had the desired results.

**What I modified and why:**
As noted above in my code block, I had to ask for further assistance in filtering apostrophes and "ing".

